// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`renderEmail > renders a turn: what was read, the story, every roll, the room, map and hero 1`] = `
"##- Reply above this line -##

DAILY DUNGEON · Turn 2 · Sunday, October 11, 2026
The Tower Entry

Your move, as I read it: Climb down the rope.

You lower yourself hand over hand into the dark. Something squeaks below.

WHAT HAPPENED
-------------
- You go down to The Tower Entry.

WHERE YOU ARE: THE TOWER ENTRY
------------------------------
The rope ends on the masonry floor of a round, roofless tower room. Rubble and old leaves cover the ground. Two giant rats startle from a nest in the debris.

Enemies:
- Giant Rat — HP 7/7 · AC 12 · attack +4, 1d4+2 · initiative 12 · spots sneaking on 10+
- Giant Rat — HP 7/7 · AC 12 · attack +4, 1d4+2 · initiative 12 · spots sneaking on 10+
Exits: north, east, west.

Map ([@] = you):
[ ]
 |
[@]

YOUR HERO: BRAKKA THE BARBARIAN (LEVEL 1)
-----------------------------------------
HP 14/14 · AC 13 · to hit +5 · damage 1d12+3 (Greataxe) · stealth +1 · perception +0 · initiative +1
Inventory: Greataxe, Handaxe x2, Explorer's pack, Health Potion x1

YOUR MOVE
---------
Reply to this email with what you do, in your own words. For example:
- Attack the giant rat. I rolled 15 to hit and 6 damage.
- Sneak past and go north.
- Dodge, and drink a potion.

Rolling real dice? Put your totals in, modifiers added. Leave them out and I'll roll for you; monsters always roll their own.
I play your latest reply at 07:00 (America/Toronto) each day, so you can change your mind until then. Reply "restart" to begin again with a new hero.

Daily Dungeon: solo D&D by email, forked from Daily Scribe.
"
`;

exports[`renderEmail > renders death and victory with a run summary and a way to play again 1`] = `
"##- Reply above this line -##

DAILY DUNGEON · Sunday, October 11, 2026
Brakka has fallen

WHAT HAPPENED
-------------
- You have fallen.

Brakka the Barbarian fell in the dark after 6 turns. Rooms explored: 1 of 6. Monsters defeated: 0.

YOUR HERO: BRAKKA THE BARBARIAN (LEVEL 1)
-----------------------------------------
HP 0/14 · AC 13 · to hit +5 · damage 1d12+3 (Greataxe) · stealth +1 · perception +0 · initiative +1
Inventory: Greataxe, Handaxe x2, Explorer's pack, Health Potion x1

CHOOSE A CLASS
--------------
- Fighter: d10 HP, chain mail + shield (AC 18), Longsword. Tough and reliable.
- Rogue: d8 HP, leather armour (AC 11 + DEX), Shortsword + bow. Expert at sneaking.
- Barbarian: d12 HP, unarmoured (AC 10 + DEX + CON), Greataxe. Big hits, big health.

Reply with a name and a class, for example “Brakka, barbarian”. If you rolled your own ability scores (STR, DEX, CON, INT, WIS, CHA), include them; anything you leave out I'll roll for you (4d6, drop the lowest). Can't decide? Reply “surprise me”.
I'll read your reply at 07:00 (America/Toronto) and your adventure begins.

Daily Dungeon: solo D&D by email, forked from Daily Scribe.
"
`;

exports[`renderEmail > renders the welcome email with the class choice and no hero yet 1`] = `
"##- Reply above this line -##

DAILY DUNGEON · Sunday, October 11, 2026
Create your hero

The Sunken Vault: A ledge overlooks a citadel sunk deep into the earth. A sturdy rope, knotted at intervals, is tied to a leaning pillar and drops into the dark below.

This is a solo Dungeons & Dragons adventure played over email, one turn a day. Each morning I send what happened and where you stand; you reply with your next move whenever suits you.

CHOOSE A CLASS
--------------
- Fighter: d10 HP, chain mail + shield (AC 18), Longsword. Tough and reliable.
- Rogue: d8 HP, leather armour (AC 11 + DEX), Shortsword + bow. Expert at sneaking.
- Barbarian: d12 HP, unarmoured (AC 10 + DEX + CON), Greataxe. Big hits, big health.

Reply with a name and a class, for example “Brakka, barbarian”. If you rolled your own ability scores (STR, DEX, CON, INT, WIS, CHA), include them; anything you leave out I'll roll for you (4d6, drop the lowest). Can't decide? Reply “surprise me”.
I'll read your reply at 07:00 (America/Toronto) and your adventure begins.

Daily Dungeon: solo D&D by email, forked from Daily Scribe.
"
`;
